-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  std_hookio_stream_text_long.adam - text mode across ucrt's fills (PaskalCPP's
  std_hookio TestStreamTextLong)

  The fixture's long samples (past the small fill, two big fills, a '\r' or
  a lone '\n' at a fill boundary, a '\r' last in the small fill after an
  fseek, a Ctrl-Z after a big fill, a number ending the first big fill)
  read from C through "rt", "r" and "rb" on a registered memory IO and on a
  real file of the same bytes: every slot of std_hookio_c_textlong (reads,
  ftell at marks, a read past a Ctrl-Z after ftell) and of
  std_hookio_c_seekfail equals the real file's. Sample 0 read "rt": one
  fread gives 450 translated bytes of its 600 (150 "\r\n" pairs).
*******************************************************************************/

